    "source": "lengthM (200.6 m overall), beamM (20.2 m) and maxSpeedMps (35 kn, converted with 1 kn = 0.514444 m/s) from the English Wikipedia article 'Mogami-class cruiser', read 2026-09-26. Japanese Monographs 145 and 149, official postwar translations, record the four-ship Mogami construction program and its conversion from 155 mm to 200 mm guns; U.S. Navy ORD-ONI 9 lists the Mogami-class 8-inch battery (primary wartime/postwar class confirmation, checked 2026-09-26). deckHeightM and turnRateRadPerS (1.5 deg/s) are ESTIMATES. hullHp (three bombs plus three rockets) is a gameplay choice. ARMAMENT (Track M, M1, read 2026-10-08): the model keeps its five-turret heavy-cruiser layout (Ruling R4; Mogami herself lost Nos. 4 and 5 in her 1943 conversion), so it carries five twin 20 cm turrets (the 1937 rearmament), four twin 12.7 cm Type 89, and the June 1944 light AA of 60 x 25 mm, 14 triple and 18 single (English Wikipedia 'Japanese cruiser Mogami (1934)'). Turrets and 12.7 cm mounts are carved at the model's own positions (axis on each barbette); the model has no 25 mm, so the 14 triples are generated kits and the singles two static galleries of nine, at ESTIMATED positions on its main deck."
